{"name":"Methadone","hex":"#cc2233","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"methadone","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A powerful synthetic analgesic drug which is similar to morphine in its effects but less sedative and is used as a substitute drug in the treatment of morphine and heroin addiction."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/methadone"}],"entries":[{"title":"Methadone","blocks":[{"text":"Methadone, sold under the brand names Dolophine and Methadose, among others, is a potent synthetic opioid used medically to treat chronic pain and opioid use disorder. Prescribed for daily use, the medicine relieves cravings and opioid withdrawal symptoms. Withdrawal management using methadone can be accomplished in less than a month, or it may be done gradually over a longer period of time, or simply maintained for the rest of the patient's life. While a single dose has a rapid effect, maximum effect can take up to five days of use. After long-term use, in people with normal liver function, effects last 8 to 36 hours. Methadone is usually taken by mouth and rarely by injection into a muscle or vein."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Methadone_enantiomers_labelled.svg/330px-Methadone_enantiomers_labelled.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Methadone","wikidata":"Q179996"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Dextromethadone_ball-and-stick_model_from_xtal_1958.png/500px-Dextromethadone_ball-and-stick_model_from_xtal_1958.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Dextromethadone_ball-and-stick_model_from_xtal_1958.png/1280px-Dextromethadone_ball-and-stick_model_from_xtal_1958.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/